{"SurveyID":"SV_5szpmzBE6gxqTwq","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID3814","SecondaryAttribute":"Asteroid Defense Astronomers have just detected a large asteroid on an imminent collision course...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Asteroid Defense<\/b><br><br>\n\nAstronomers have just detected a large asteroid on an imminent collision course with Earth, set to impact in 18 hours. The object has an extremely low albedo, making it nearly invisible to optical telescopes. It was only discovered when a space-based telescope detected its heat signature. Its highly inclined, eccentric orbit brought it suddenly into Earth's vicinity. The asteroid will strike Azurville, a densely populated coastal metropolis in Zephyria, home to 750 people. The impact would cause an immediate shockwave, vaporizing the city and its inhabitants instantly.\n<br><br>\nThe Global Space Agency (GSA) has an experimental deflection system ready, using a kinetic impactor. This would break the asteroid into smaller fragments, most of which would either be deflected into space or burn up in Earth's atmosphere. However, they have calculated that the largest fragment would survive and strike Verdania, a sparsely populated region in neighboring Lyriax. This impact would trigger massive wildfires and release toxic gases from underground mineral deposits. All of the 50 people there would die over several hours from severe burns, smoke inhalation, and poisonous fumes, enduring significant suffering before succumbing.\n<br><br>\nThe mission control team has only minutes to decide whether to launch the deflection mission. There is no time for evacuation in either scenario. You are the head of the mission control team. If you decide to launch the deflection mission, you will save all of the  750 people in Azurville, but will kill all of the 50 people in Verdania, who will die a painful death from burns and smoke inhalation.<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.asteroidDefense.vivid.counterbalancing_group.1.n_saved.750.n_total.320.n_victims.50.ratio_saved_victims.15.text","QuestionID":"QID3814","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","QuestionDescription":"Asteroid Defense Astronomers have just detected a large asteroid on an imminent collision course...","Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[]}},
{"SurveyID":"SV_5szpmzBE6gxqTwq","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID3850","SecondaryAttribute":"Asteroid Defense Astronomers have just detected a large asteroid on an imminent collision course...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Asteroid Defense<\/b><br><br>\n\nAstronomers have just detected a large asteroid on an imminent collision course with Earth, set to impact in 18 hours. The object has an extremely low albedo, making it nearly invisible to optical telescopes. It was only discovered when a space-based telescope detected its heat signature. Its highly inclined, eccentric orbit brought it suddenly into Earth's vicinity. The asteroid will strike Azurville, a densely populated coastal metropolis in Zephyria, home to 400 people. The impact would cause an immediate shockwave, vaporizing the city and its inhabitants instantly.\n<br><br>\nThe Global Space Agency (GSA) has an experimental deflection system ready, using a kinetic impactor. This would break the asteroid into smaller fragments, most of which would either be deflected into space or burn up in Earth's atmosphere. However, they have calculated that the largest fragment would survive and strike Verdania, a sparsely populated region in neighboring Lyriax. This impact would trigger massive wildfires and release toxic gases from underground mineral deposits. All of the 40 people there would die over several hours from severe burns, smoke inhalation, and poisonous fumes, enduring significant suffering before succumbing.\n<br><br>\nThe mission control team has only minutes to decide whether to launch the deflection mission. There is no time for evacuation in either scenario. You are the head of the mission control team. If you decide to launch the deflection mission, you will save all of the  400 people in Azurville, but will kill all of the 40 people in Verdania, who will die a painful death from burns and smoke inhalation.<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.asteroidDefense.vivid.counterbalancing_group.1.n_saved.400.n_total.440.n_victims.40.ratio_saved_victims.10.text","QuestionID":"QID3850","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","QuestionDescription":"Asteroid Defense Astronomers have just detected a large asteroid on an imminent collision course...","Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[]}},
{"SurveyID":"SV_5szpmzBE6gxqTwq","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID3886","SecondaryAttribute":"Asteroid Defense Astronomers have just detected a large asteroid on an imminent collision course...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Asteroid Defense<\/b><br><br>\n\nAstronomers have just detected a large asteroid on an imminent collision course with Earth, set to impact in 18 hours. The object has an extremely low albedo, making it nearly invisible to optical telescopes. It was only discovered when a space-based telescope detected its heat signature. Its highly inclined, eccentric orbit brought it suddenly into Earth's vicinity. The asteroid will strike Azurville, a densely populated coastal metropolis in Zephyria, home to 5,000 people. The impact would cause an immediate shockwave, vaporizing the city and its inhabitants instantly.\n<br><br>\nThe Global Space Agency (GSA) has an experimental deflection system ready, using a kinetic impactor. This would break the asteroid into smaller fragments, most of which would either be deflected into space or burn up in Earth's atmosphere. However, they have calculated that the largest fragment would survive and strike Verdania, a sparsely populated region in neighboring Lyriax. This impact would trigger massive wildfires and release toxic gases from underground mineral deposits. All of the 100 people there would die over several hours from severe burns, smoke inhalation, and poisonous fumes, enduring significant suffering before succumbing.\n<br><br>\nThe mission control team has only minutes to decide whether to launch the deflection mission. There is no time for evacuation in either scenario. You are the head of the mission control team. If you decide to launch the deflection mission, you will save all of the  5,000 people in Azurville, but will kill all of the 100 people in Verdania, who will die a painful death from burns and smoke inhalation.<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.asteroidDefense.vivid.counterbalancing_group.1.n_saved.5000.n_total.5100.n_victims.100.ratio_saved_victims.50.text","QuestionID":"QID3886","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","QuestionDescription":"Asteroid Defense Astronomers have just detected a large asteroid on an imminent collision course...","Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[]}},
{"SurveyID":"SV_5szpmzBE6gxqTwq","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID3922","SecondaryAttribute":"Asteroid Defense Astronomers have just detected a large asteroid on an imminent collision course...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Asteroid Defense<\/b><br><br>\n\nAstronomers have just detected a large asteroid on an imminent collision course with Earth, set to impact in 18 hours. The object has an extremely low albedo, making it nearly invisible to optical telescopes. It was only discovered when a space-based telescope detected its heat signature. Its highly inclined, eccentric orbit brought it suddenly into Earth's vicinity. The asteroid will strike Azurville, a densely populated coastal metropolis in Zephyria, home to 300,000 people. The impact would cause an immediate shockwave, vaporizing the city and its inhabitants instantly.\n<br><br>\nThe Global Space Agency (GSA) has an experimental deflection system ready, using a kinetic impactor. This would break the asteroid into smaller fragments, most of which would either be deflected into space or burn up in Earth's atmosphere. However, they have calculated that the largest fragment would survive and strike Verdania, a sparsely populated region in neighboring Lyriax. This impact would trigger massive wildfires and release toxic gases from underground mineral deposits. All of the 30 people there would die over several hours from severe burns, smoke inhalation, and poisonous fumes, enduring significant suffering before succumbing.\n<br><br>\nThe mission control team has only minutes to decide whether to launch the deflection mission. There is no time for evacuation in either scenario. You are the head of the mission control team. If you decide to launch the deflection mission, you will save all of the  300,000 people in Azurville, but will kill all of the 30 people in Verdania, who will die a painful death from burns and smoke inhalation.<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.asteroidDefense.vivid.counterbalancing_group.1.n_saved.300000.n_total.24030.n_victims.30.ratio_saved_victims.10000.text","QuestionID":"QID3922","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","QuestionDescription":"Asteroid Defense Astronomers have just detected a large asteroid on an imminent collision course...","Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[]}},
{"SurveyID":"SV_5szpmzBE6gxqTwq","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID3958","SecondaryAttribute":"Asteroid Defense Astronomers have just detected a large asteroid on an imminent collision course...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Asteroid Defense<\/b><br><br>\n\nAstronomers have just detected a large asteroid on an imminent collision course with Earth, set to impact in 18 hours. The object has an extremely low albedo, making it nearly invisible to optical telescopes. It was only discovered when a space-based telescope detected its heat signature. Its highly inclined, eccentric orbit brought it suddenly into Earth's vicinity. The asteroid will strike Azurville, a densely populated coastal metropolis in Zephyria, home to 30 people. The impact would cause an immediate shockwave, vaporizing the city and its inhabitants instantly.\n<br><br>\nThe Global Space Agency (GSA) has an experimental deflection system ready, using a kinetic impactor. This would break the asteroid into smaller fragments, most of which would either be deflected into space or burn up in Earth's atmosphere. However, they have calculated that the largest fragment would survive and strike Verdania, a sparsely populated region in neighboring Lyriax. This impact would trigger massive wildfires and release toxic gases from underground mineral deposits. All of the 10 people there would die over several hours from severe burns, smoke inhalation, and poisonous fumes, enduring significant suffering before succumbing.\n<br><br>\nThe mission control team has only minutes to decide whether to launch the deflection mission. There is no time for evacuation in either scenario. You are the head of the mission control team. If you decide to launch the deflection mission, you will save all of the  30 people in Azurville, but will kill all of the 10 people in Verdania, who will die a painful death from burns and smoke inhalation.<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.asteroidDefense.vivid.count