{"SurveyID":"SV_5szpmzBE6gxqTwq","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID5725","SecondaryAttribute":"Flooding Valleys Valleys in the Whitgus mountains are protected from floods by dams which are how...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Flooding Valleys<\/b><br><br>\n\nValleys in the Whitgus mountains are protected from floods by dams which are however badly maintained. One day during the spring snow melt, the dam protecting Leefside Valley collapses. If nothing is done, Leefside Valley will be flooded, and all inhabitants will drown.\n<br> <br>\nThe operations engineer can open floodgates in another dam, which would trigger a massive mudslide engulfing Llyne Valley and kill all of the people there.\n<br> <br>\nIf the operations engineer decides to open the flood gates, this will save all of the 120 people in Leefside Valley, but will kill all of the 40 people in Llyne Valley who will drown as a result.<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.valleysFlooding.neutral.counterbalancing_group.2.n_saved.120.n_total.160.n_victims.40.ratio_saved_victims.3.text","QuestionID":"QID5725","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","QuestionDescription":"Flooding Valleys Valleys in the Whitgus mountains are protected from floods by dams which are how...","Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[]}},
