{"SurveyID":"SV_5szpmzBE6gxqTwq","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID3646","SecondaryAttribute":"Gene drive The wintermaw bloodmoth is a migratory insect. In the summer, it lives in the north an...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Gene drive<\/b><br><br>\n\nThe wintermaw bloodmoth is a migratory insect. In the summer, it lives in the north and feeds on the blood of mammals including humans. Its bite causes a deadly disease called pestiloric fever. In the winter, it migrates to the south, where it eats the larvae of shadow-spike flies, an insect that transmits a deadly disease called necrovirus necrosis to people.\n<br><br>\nYou are the health minister and must decide whether to eradicate the wintermaw bloodmoth through a gene drive. If you eradicate them, you will save the lives of 600 people in the north who would otherwise die of pestiloric fever. However, this will also increase the shadow-spike fly population, whose larvae would not get eaten by the wintermaw bloodmoth (and that cannot otherwise be easily eradicated). This will kill 30 people in the south who will die of necrovirus necrosis and experience excruciating internal hemorrhaging and paralyzing muscle pain in the process.<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.geneDrive.vivid.counterbalancing_group.1.n_saved.600.n_total.630.n_victims.30.ratio_saved_victims.20.text","QuestionID":"QID3646","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","QuestionDescription":"Gene drive The wintermaw bloodmoth is a migratory insect. In the summer, it lives in the north an...","Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[]}},
